<speak>She has taken over the main diary, thankfully. Before that, I was receiving messages from different people and trying to remember which conversation belonged to which meeting. My brother would tell me something over lunch, then assume it had gone into the office diary. My cousin would tell the receptionist a different time. Now my niece insists that appointments go through the same channel. She is polite about it, but firmer than I used to be, and it seems to be working.</speak>